---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../../lib/siteUrl';
import '../../../styles/docs-prose.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Comic Lettering — Varve Docs"
  description="Create and edit comic balloons in Varve while keeping dialogue, tails, and page artwork editable."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <main class="docs-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/docs')}>Documentation</a> / Tools / Comic Lettering
      </nav>
      <h1 class="site-page-title">Comic Lettering</h1>
      <p class="docs-intro">
        Varve builds a balloon from ordinary text, shape, and path nodes. The words remain editable,
        and the balloon uses the same selection, history, layer, and export systems as other artwork.
        Comic support is a built foundation inside the existing workspaces, not a separate Comic
        workspace.
      </p>

      <section class="docs-section">
        <h2>Create a speech balloon</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Create or select one text object that is not already inside a balloon.</li>
          <li>In the Inspector, open <strong>Typography</strong> and choose <strong>Add speech balloon</strong>.</li>
          <li>The selected text is grouped with an editable balloon body and tail. The text is moved into the group rather than flattened or duplicated.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          Select the group to open the <strong>Comic balloon</strong> Inspector section. Choose Speech,
          Thought, Caption, Whisper, Shout, Burst, or Cloud; adjust padding and line shape; then edit
          the tail endpoint, curve, or width. Add, flip, remove, or detach a tail from the same
          section. Double-click the balloon to edit its dialogue.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="docs-section">
        <h2>Choose how dialogue fits</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Reflow in balloon</strong> wraps the text to the balloon and reports when it is near the edge.</li>
          <li><strong>Fit balloon to text</strong> grows the body around the current text.</li>
          <li><strong>Show overflow</strong> leaves the text size and balloon geometry in place and reports the overflow.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Fitting never silently reduces the font size. For round balloons, the first and last lines
          can narrow to follow the contour. Vertical writing remains rectangular. Check long
          translations and exported lettering at the final size.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="docs-section">
        <h2>Current boundaries</h2>
        <p>
          A dedicated canvas drag tool for drawing balloons, joined balloons with a shared outline,
          vertical contour columns, speaker-target placement, and script-import automation are not
          included. Tails added manually to Burst or Cloud recipes anchor at the text box; tails
          created with the balloon start at the shaped outline. Comic page profiles and panels are
          editable starting points, not publisher-specific export guarantees.
        </p>
        <p>
          See the <a href={sitePath('/features/comic-lettering')}>Comic Lettering feature page</a>{' '}
          for the full capability and status summary, and <a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/typography')}>Typography</a>{' '}
          for shared text controls.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>
